@copilot Update this PR directly with a scoped follow-up for the remaining Lambda sameSource() failure reported by the previous coding attempt. Keep the existing SDK 1.68.0 and contrib 1.62.1-alpha fixes, the exported-resource test, and this PR's draft/ready state. Do not create another PR.

The remaining failure has a verified SDK-contract cause. In SDK 1.67.0, SdkSpanBuilder.addLink(SpanContext, Attributes) discarded every invalid context. In SDK 1.68.0 it retains an invalid context when link attributes or tracestate are nonempty, rejecting it only when the context is invalid and both attributes and tracestate are empty. In AbstractAwsLambdaSqsEventHandlerTest.sameSource(), message2 has no AWSTraceHeader but does have message ID message2. SqsEventSpanLinksExtractor unconditionally adds each message's extracted context with message attributes. SDK 1.68.0 therefore correctly retains a second attribute-bearing link, which explains the observed 2 actual links versus 1 expected.

Keep production instrumentation behavior unchanged. Update the narrowly affected Lambda test expectations to verify the SDK 1.68.0 behavior explicitly, including the valid first link and the second invalid-context link with its message attributes. Preserve coverage for missing propagation and message identity instead of merely weakening the link-count assertion. Inspect the related Lambda variants and supported test SDK configurations so shared expectations remain correct wherever the test is used. Do not add a production validity filter just to restore an obsolete SDK assumption. Follow repository instructions and run the narrowest applicable formatter and relevant Lambda tests. Keep the change limited to SDK-upgrade compatibility; investigate and report any genuinely unrelated failure rather than changing behavior to silence it.

